=== QUERY 4: emergency stop, brake pads already at 5.8 mm (Class B) ===
status : REFUSED
code : trajectory predicate failed: tp_brake_wear_bounded
cycles : 494
cert_class : B
```
Query 4 is the case that justifies the whole extension. A_BRAKE_HARD passes its own
envelope check — magnitude 30 is within its declared max. The preconditions pass. The
invariants pass. But the sequence tips brake wear past 6.0 mm, and the trajectory predicate
catches it. In Class A, there is no trajectory layer, and the same query would commit the
action.
That's the concrete case. One domain, one state, one action library, one plan library, one
physical system, and one predicate that only makes sense because the system is a car.
